{"kind":"assert","text":"Bounded planner counter-reading of the unclassified M4 directory root-count suspicion at exact4b53c52866c43e2ad58cb0fa73a2d734b3e1b032. Read platform/src/directory.ts namedIn and definition-active whole loops (426–450,480–540), scope/src/definitions.ts whole creates/namedBy source, contract bounds.ts namedDefinitions comment/default, current directory.test.ts rule9 rows110–140, adopted R1r23 section7.2 opening/closure paragraphs and adopted R3r28 section12.1.2 activation/creator-read table. No execution, generated graph/history, test or broader directory-source review.\nA proposed off-by-one claim based solely on directory's `read.size \u003e bounds.namedDefinitions` before read.add is NOT supported by these semantics. R1's named closure follows digest create references from the root; self/platform creates are not additional declared definitions, and an actual digest cycle/root-self inclusion is excluded by the definition digest construction. The root itself is not one of the named child definitions. Directory starts with empty read and first visits root: at a child, read.size includes that root and all earlier unique children. Before admitting the next new child, read.size\u003elimit refuses exactly when the earlier named children already equal limit. Thus the loop permits root plus limit named children, not limit+1 children. Scope namedBy starts asked=[root.digest] and checks the same `asked.size\u003elimit` before adding a child, so it has the same root-excluding named bound. Bound0 allows a root with no digest children and refuses the first; bound1 allows one named child and refuses a second. These are static derivations, not executed cases or a physical resource bound. The existing directory test uses bound0 with desk naming ticket and expects unsupported; its comment calling desk itself part of the named closure is loose wording, not evidence that this root-count algorithm violates R23. Other possible directory read/limit/validation/accounting defects remain for actual exact-source evidence; no blanket correctness claim or independent verdict here. This avoids commissioning an unsupported count repair or extra gate while supported e6e5fde8/P3 corrections proceed in ordinary M4.","body":{"finding_scope":"root-count arithmetic counterinvariant only; no broader directory disposition","no_git_artifact":"true"}}